</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Pronunciation-guided context learning</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Instead of relying solely on conventional grapheme-only context <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> for LLM-based ASR, we propose a pronunciation-guided context construction strategy to explicitly incorporate pronunciation information and improve keyword recognition. Specifically, each word <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is paired with its corresponding grapheme-to-phoneme transcription <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, forming the interleaved grapheme-phoneme context <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{gp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{gp}</annotation></semantics></math>. As illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ PAC: Pronunciation-Aware Contextualized Large Language Model-based Automatic Speech Recognition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, given <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{g}=\text{``speech, PAC''}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>“speech, PAC”</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{g}=\text{``speech, PAC''}</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{gp}=\text{``speech (S P IY1 CH), PAC (P AE1 K)''}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>“speech (S P IY1 CH), PAC (P AE1 K)”</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{gp}=\text{``speech (S P IY1 CH), PAC (P AE1 K)''}</annotation></semantics></math>, where phoneme annotations are generated using the grapheme-to-phoneme toolkit<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://pypi.org/project/g2p-en/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://pypi.org/project/g2p-en/</a></span></span></span> for English and the pypinyin toolkit<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://pypi.org/project/pypinyin/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://pypi.org/project/pypinyin/</a></span></span></span> for Mandarin.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, our experiments show that simply providing <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{gp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{gp}</annotation></semantics></math> offers limited improvement over grapheme-only context, as the model may still focus on graphemic information and fail to fully exploit pronunciation cues. To address this limitation, we introduce an augmented guided context <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{gpgd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{gpgd}</annotation></semantics></math> by adding grapheme-only distractor words <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with similar or identical pronunciations to the target keywords in the label <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, for “speech (S P IY1 CH), PAC (P AE1 K)”, we add the homophone distractor “pack” to form “speech (S P IY1 CH), PAC (P AE1 K), pack”. This structure encourages the model to actively leverage contextual phonemic information, thereby improving recognition of the target keyword “PAC” in <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>, we employ hand-crafted linguistic rules to identify spelling alternatives with similar phonetic patterns for English, while for Mandarin, homophone replacement is performed using the pypinyin toolkit to substitute words with identical pronunciations. The construction process for pronunciation-guided context is summarized in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ PAC: Pronunciation-Aware Contextualized Large Language Model-based Automatic Speech Recognition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=P_{2}=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=P_{2}=1/3</annotation></semantics></math> are set to balance the distribution of different context types during training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To optimize the model with diverse contextual inputs, we define the Cross-Entropy (CE) losses for the aggregate context types as:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S3.E1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:109.0pt;height:13.1pt;vertical-align:-7.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-13.6pt,1.6pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
<p id="S3.E1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.E1.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{PGCL}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C})=\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C}_{g})}_{\mathcal{L}_{g}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C}_{gp})}_{\mathcal{L}_{gp}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C}_{gpgd})}_{\mathcal{L}_{gpgd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>PGCL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{PGCL}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C})=\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C}_{g})}_{\mathcal{L}_{g}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C}_{gp})}_{\mathcal{L}_{gp}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbf{Y}|\mathbf{X},\mathbf{C}_{gpgd})}_{\mathcal{L}_{gpgd}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the standard cross-entropy loss.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of PAC and baseline methods on Mandarin AISHELL-1 test sets. “NA” indicates no biasing keywords, “GT” refers to ground-truth keyword biasing, and <math id="S3.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the bias list size.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S3.T2.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:165.6pt;height:97.2pt;vertical-align:-47.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-123.7pt,72.6pt) scale(0.401038519695376,0.401038519695376) ;">
<table id="S3.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S3.T2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Setting</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="2">SeACo-Paraformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="2">CFL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="2">PAC (Ours)</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">CER</td>
